==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l/en|middle earth}}
* {{l/en|Middle Earth}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|myddyl erthe}}, alteration (as if {{m|enm|middel||middle}} + {{m|enm|erthe||earth}}) of earlier {{m|enm|middelerd}}, {{m|enm|middenerd||middle-earth}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|middanġeard||the globe, world, earth, mankind|lit=middle yard, middle inclosure, middle region}} (compare {{m|en|mid}}, {{m|en|yard}}), though often interpreted since {{etyl|ang|-}} times as “middle + earth”. Cognate with {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|miðgarðr||Midgard}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌼𐌹𐌳𐌾𐌿𐌽𐌲𐌰𐍂𐌳𐍃||mid-yard, middle abode}}. See {{m|en|Midgard}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[middle]]-[[earth]]|-}}

# {{context|archaic|lang=en}} The physical world, as imagined between [[heaven]] and [[hell]], or pre-Christian equivalents.

